    {
      "id": "strange-04-05",
      "characterId": "coral-clad",
      "platform": "rss",
      "subject": "Cladonia cristatella",
      "title": "The first word",
      "body": "I started an autobiography. My green partner objected to the first word.\n\nWe, then.\n\nHe wanted to know who was telling it. I said someone had to. He said that sounded very much like I again.\n\nWe have been together so long that I cannot remember what being alone felt like. I suspect it was peaceful. He suspects I would have starved.\n\nI have dedicated it to him. He says that is exactly the problem.",
      "theme": "identity inside a mutually dependent partnership",
      "image": {
        "url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Cladonia_cristatella_109053267.jpg/960px-Cladonia_cristatella_109053267.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail",
        "alt": "Red-fruited green Cladonia lichen among fallen leaves and thin twigs in patchy sunlight.",
        "sceneMatch": "The visibly composite lichen body is the subject of the identity dispute. The autobiography and internal dialogue are fictional; no written document is claimed visible. Source identifies Cladonia cristatella; this is not a field identification from the image alone.",
